{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>To fight, etc. To save, etc.</b> The meaning of <b>to fight</b> etc. is — to destroy your enemies. And His saying <b>to save</b> etc. means that not a single one of the children of Israel should die in the war, and this is the essence of the miracle — that the war should go heavily against their enemies and not a single one of the children of Israel should fall. Or perhaps to this He intended in what He said at the beginning of the verse, <b>HaShem your Elohim</b> — He alluded to mercy and to judgment: mercy to save Israel, judgment to destroy their enemies. And without this, it would have been sufficient for Him to say ״כִּי אֱלֹהֵיכֶם הוֹלֵךְ״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:18:10.316206054Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}